{"step_index":9,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-17T16:02:26Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nSPECIAL TESTS I. TESTS FOR CIRCULATION & SWELLING 1. ALLEN TEST Purpose To assess the patency of the radial and ulnar arteries. Procedure • • • • Patient clenches the fist. Compress both radial and ulnar arteries. Patient opens the hand. Release one artery at a time and observe colour return. Positive Sign Delayed or absent return of normal hand colour. Indicates Arterial insufficiency or vascular occlusion. 2. DIGITAL BLOOD FLOW TEST Purpose To assess circulation to the fingers. Procedure • • Compress the fingertip until it blanches. Release the pressure. Positive Sign Delayed capillary refill (>2 seconds). Indicates Reduced peripheral circulation. 3. FIGURE-OF-8 MEASUREMENT Purpose To assess hand and wrist swelling (edema). Procedure • Use a measuring tape in a standardized figure-of-8 pattern around the wrist and hand. Record the measurement. 1 • Positive Finding Increased measurement compared with the opposite side. Indicates Hand or wrist edema. 4. HAND VOLUME TEST Purpose To assess hand edema. Procedure • • Immerse the hand into a volumeter filled with water. Measure the volume of displaced water. Positive Finding Increased displaced volume. Indicates Hand swelling/edema. II. TESTS FOR THORACIC OUTLET SYNDROME 1. ADSON'S TEST Purpose To assess Thoracic Outlet Syndrome (TOS). Procedure • • Palpate the radial pulse. Patient extends the neck, rotates the head toward the tested side, and takes a deep breath. Positive Sign Reduced/absent radial pulse or reproduction of symptoms. Indicates Thoracic Outlet Syndrome. 2. ROOS STRESS TEST (EAST) Purpose To assess Thoracic Outlet Syndrome. Procedure Patient abducts shoulders to 90°, externally rotates them, and flexes elbows to 90°. 2 • Patient repeatedly opens and closes the hands for 3 minutes. Positive Sign Pain, numbness, tingling, heaviness, or inability to continue. Indicates Thoracic Outlet Syndrome.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-17T21:32:26+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
